RERELEASE=1
DESCRIPTION=FL-02 stage 2: KeyQuorum-signed file histories in the freestanding image, kept on the image's data disk. The bss moves above 1 MiB (linker.ld links it at FL_KERNEL_BSS_ADDR, 0x100000, and never loads it); stage 2 refuses to boot unless one usable E820 entry holds it (FLINTSTONE_BOOT_FAIL bss-memory), the boot info reserves the image and the bss as two ranges, and fl_bootinfo_validate checks both, so the loaded image ends at 0x8bb60 (0x87440 security lab) with room below 0x9f000. The kernel stack grows to 24 KiB (0xa000). The checkpoints run in the default image over the in-memory storage table kq_mem_storage.c, and the store is persisted to the second IDE disk (kq_disk.c, ATA PIO on the secondary master): an append-only log of records, each a header sector (magic, kind, name, length, CRC-32) written last after its data sectors, read at boot before the accounts are enrolled, with a damaged record ending the log. Histories (kind 1) and sealed account keys (kind 2) persist, so a signed history still verifies after a reboot and the default accounts keep their keys. Commands: server file sign (asks for the password, opens the sealed key for that one signature, wipes it), log, verify; the image prints CAP keyquorum-disk=present|absent and CAP keyquorum-history=ok after a boot self-test. The placement layer, the shared folder gate and the container mutex are hosted-only; kq_platform.c supplies the libc subset and the clock as KeyQuorum UTC text; fl_fs_join_path and the reserved-suffix check are shared header inlines; the image trust table holds 8 signers. Tests: test_kq_checkpoint, test_fs_bootmap, make test-freestanding-kq-history, make test-freestanding-kq-persist (reboot restore, damaged record, no disk); test-freestanding-shell and test_freestanding_entry unchanged and passing. The security-lab image (SECFEAT=1) now includes the same KeyQuorum code, sealed keys, data disk and fw_cfg entropy: the build script refuses a payload over the loader limit (1144 sectors below 0x9f000) rather than a fixed 1024, and the security-lab payload is 1027 sectors (image end 0x90488).



RELEASE_DATE=2026-11-17
